---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/base';

const lastUpdated = '20 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How PS Laser collects, uses, stores, and protects data — grounded in the app's actual implementation, including authentication, Firestore, Cloudflare, Backblaze B2, Google Drive, OpenRouter, and FCM."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="last-updated reveal">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2>Who operates this app</h2>
        <p>
          PS Laser<br />
          Gat No. 753, Velu Bag, Tal-Bhor<br />
          Pune – 412205, Maharashtra, India<br />
          GST: 27ABHFP5667Q1Z8<br />
          Phone: +91 77199 76990<br />
          Support: <a href="mailto:pslaser24@gmail.com">pslaser24@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          PS Laser is an internal manufacturing operations application used by PS Laser's own
          staff (Owners, Managers, Supervisors, and Workers) to manage orders, production, and
          delivery. It is not a consumer-facing app, and customers do not create accounts or
          log in themselves.
        </p>

        <h2>Data we collect</h2>
        <h3>Employee (staff user) data</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Name, role, department, shift</li>
          <li>
            A login PIN — never stored in plain text. It is converted to a one-way cryptographic
            hash (scrypt) before being written to a storage location that no user, including an
            Owner, can read directly through the app.
          </li>
          <li>
            A security question and answer, used only to recover access if a PIN is forgotten.
            The answer is hashed the same way the PIN is.
          </li>
          <li>A device push-notification token, tied to your account and device, used to deliver notifications.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Customer / client data (entered by staff, about your customers)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Client name, phone number, email address, billing/delivery address, and GST number, where provided</li>
          <li>Order details: items, quantities, pricing, due dates, and an optional reference photo</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="callout">
          Order and client records are retained as financial and business records and are not
          deleted on request — cancelling an order is used instead of deleting it. This mirrors
          standard bookkeeping practice for a manufacturing business and is explained further
          under "Data retention" below.
        </div>

        <h2>How we use data</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To operate the core functions of the app — orders, production tracking, delivery, and reporting.</li>
          <li>To send push notifications about order events, delivery reminders, and job assignments.</li>
          <li>
            To power the in-app AI assistant: when you ask it a question, a summary of relevant
            operational data (such as order status, due dates, and — where relevant to your
            question — client name and delivery address) is sent to our AI provider,
            OpenRouter, to generate a response. Phone numbers, email addresses, GST numbers, and
            other long numeric identifiers are automatically stripped before this data is sent.
            Client names and delivery addresses are <strong>not</strong> currently stripped when
            they're relevant to answering your question — we're disclosing this plainly rather
            than describing the process as fully anonymized.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Third-party services we use</h2>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Service</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Firebase Authentication</td><td>Signs you into the app after your PIN is verified</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Cloud Firestore</td><td>Primary application database</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Firebase Cloud Messaging</td><td>Delivers push notifications to your device</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Firebase Crashlytics</td><td>Crash reporting in release builds only, to help us fix bugs. No advertising or usage-analytics SDK is used anywhere in the app.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Cloudflare Workers</td><td>Our application backend — handles login, notifications, and the AI assistant proxy</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Backblaze B2</td><td>Stores order reference images while an order is active</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Google Drive</td><td>A dedicated business Google account (not any user's personal account) archives older order reference images after a retention period</td></tr>
              <tr><td>OpenRouter</td><td>Processes AI assistant chat requests (see "How we use data" above)</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          Order, client, and financial records are retained indefinitely as business and
          legal/financial records — this matches standard accounting-record practice, and
          orders are cancelled rather than deleted. Order reference images move from active
          storage to long-term archive storage after 90 days once an order is complete or
          cancelled, and remain in archive storage after that (no further automatic deletion
          currently occurs). Login-attempt and rate-limiting records are used only for security
          purposes and are not accessible to any user through the app.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices &amp; account deletion</h2>
        <p>
          See our dedicated <a href={withBase('/delete-account')}>Delete Account</a> page for exactly what
          deleting your account covers today, what business records are retained regardless,
          and how to request it.
        </p>

        <h2>Camera &amp; photo library access</h2>
        <p>
          The app requests camera access to scan QR codes and to take reference photos for
          orders, and photo-library access to attach an existing photo to an order. Neither
          permission is used for anything beyond these two purposes.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          PS Laser is an internal business tool for our own staff and is not directed at, or
          knowingly used by, children.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          PINs and security-question answers are never stored in plain text. Application
          secrets (API keys, service credentials) are held only on our backend and are never
          shipped inside the app. Repeated failed login attempts are automatically rate-limited.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes in a way that materially affects how your data is handled,
          we'll update the "last updated" date above.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or how your data is handled: <a href="mailto:pslaser24@gmail.com">pslaser24@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vh, 64px) 0;
  }
</style>
